<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20188" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hălys</span></b> , yos,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἅλυς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river in Asia Minor</i>, <i>flowing
				between Paphlagonia and Cappadocia</i>, now <i>Kisil-Irmak</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">secundum Halyn,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					1, 19, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 2, 2, § 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 3, 3, § 8</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circa Halyn,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 38, 16, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Croesus Halym penetrans magnam pervertet opum
					vim,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 2, 56, 115</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Croeso fatalis Halys,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					3, 272</span></i>
			.—<i>Acc.</i>: Halym, also <i><span class="en">Curt. 4,
				11, 3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A man's name</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 2,
				574</span></i>.—As a <i>surname</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 877, 9</span></i>.</div>
